WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.510 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  tens of thousands of people in the east  of the democratic republic of congo have  fled their homes in fear of their lives  it was m23 rebels that were chasing us  the m23 rebel group has taken several  small towns  some of the residents have fled to  neighbouring uganda others towards the  regional capital gomer  churches and schools like this one are  overrun with people seeking shelter  we saw people being killed by stray  bullets and those who could save  themselves are here  the congolese army has launched a  counter-offensive and retaken some of  the territory  congo's government says neighbouring  rwanda is behind m23 supporting it with  weapons and soldiers rwanda denies it  we as the government don't believe that  the m23 rebels themselves have the  military equipment which they claim to  have on the ground according to the  reports from our soldiers this is why  our suspicion of foreign support is  confirmed  ten years ago m23 took control of  swathes of eastern congo un  investigators said it was backed by  rwanda congo's army eventually defeated  them with military support from the un  and other african countries  this time congo's army has struggled to  contain the attacks launched by m23 over  the last six months  both uganda and rwanda have been accused  of fueling congo's conflicts and looting  minerals ever since they invaded in the  1990s a recent attempt to get the three  presidents together for talks in kenya's  capital nairobi failed to produce  results  the violence and humanitarian crisis are  growing and the un says it's deeply  concerned  malcolm webb al jazeera

